# Plan (opus, strong)

## Goal

Inside a simulation, a prompt held by the seat that is not acting should get its answerer's best answer, not `legal_actions(..)[0]`. This covers `simulate`'s `max_auto_answers` loop and every prompt in `simulate_reply`, including the AI's own prompts off its turn. The answerer tries its first K answers, where K is the new constant `AI_SEARCH.max_auto_answer_options` (4). Each answer tried costs one node of the shared counter and is scored by `evaluate` from the answerer's seat on the determinization (R185). One helper, `best_auto_answer`, serves both call sites. `max_auto_answers` still bounds the chain, so a step costs at most 1 + surcharge + 8 × 4 nodes. The greedy baseline keeps taking the first answer (`simulate_first_answers`), so the yardstick the gates measure against does not move.

## Files to touch

| File | New / change | What changes |
|---|---|---|
| `crates/ai/src/config.rs` | change | `AiSearch.max_auto_answer_options: i32`; `AI_SEARCH` sets it to 4 |
| `crates/ai/src/simulate.rs` | change | header line; new `pub(crate) fn best_auto_answer`; `simulate` wraps new private `simulate_answering`; new `pub fn simulate_first_answers`; the loop calls the helper |
| `crates/ai/src/reply.rs` | change | imports; `simulate_reply`'s pending branch calls the helper; its doc comment |
| `crates/ai/src/baselines.rs` | change | `greedy_action` calls `simulate_first_answers`; import; one comment |
| `crates/ai/tests/ai/lethal.rs` | change | `play_out`'s counter sized for K answers per prompt |
| `crates/ai/tests/ai/prompts_v020.rs` | change | new `mod auto_answers_the_answerers_best`, four tests |
| `docs/polish/3-ai.md` | change | `AI_SEARCH` listing, `simulate` and `simulateReply` doc comments, `simulateFirstAnswers` |

Must not touch: `spec/` (no ruling: this is the AI's internal model, not a rule), `crates/engine/`, `crates/cards/`, `crates/tools/`, `crates/server/`, `apps/web/`, manifests, `scripts/`, `.github/`, `.harness/`, `.squishy/`, `bot/`. Governing: SPEC §9.9 (Search; The opponent's reply; Quality gates), R185; R82 and R345 for the tests' setup.

