# Plan (opus, strong)

## Goal

The AI's model of a position catches up with the engine, inside `crates/ai/` only. `search_signature` starts signing the axes the issue lists: each side's mana maximum, `next_turn_mod` and `perm_mod`; zone `locks`; player `mods`; the `turn_log` counts; `fatigue_count`, `jade`, `extra_turns` and `hand_cap`; the graveyard, the exile and `backrow_piles`; the card `memory`, `tuning` and enchantments of cards off the field; the game's `delayed` effects and `marks`. Each new part appears only when it is not the default (R1224's encoding) and does not depend on order, and the lane stays out. `damage_past_taunts` soaks each Taunt one §4.4 hit at a time: Armor comes off each hit, Poisonous destroys, Trample overflow reaches the hero, a First Strike Taunt kills first, and a Reborn Taunt binds again. Each half is screened on `improve-dev` against the build before it and kept when it does not lose.

A planner run built this whole change in a scratch copy at the base commit, with the code and tests below. Results: the 25 new tests pass, and 23 of them fail on the old code (the plain-position and order tests pass on both, by design). `cargo test -p jackioh-ai` passes (309 / 55 / 13, the `merged > 200` floor included). `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo clippy -p jackioh-ai --all-targets -- -D warnings` are clean. Every R-id cited exists.

## Files to touch

| File | New/change | What changes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `crates/ai/src/simulate.rs` | change | new `sorted`, `rides_signature`, `push_side_parts`; `card_signature`, `unit_play_signature`, `search_signature` (+ doc); import `TurnLog`, `max_mana_for` |
| `crates/ai/src/evaluate.rs` | change | new `REBORN_HEALTH`, `falls_to_first_strike`, `reborn_body`; `damage_past_taunts` soak loop and doc; `face_threat` doc; import `pierces`, `reset_instance`, `takes_strike_back` |
| `crates/ai/tests/ai/position_model.rs` | new | `mod signature` (20 tests), `mod soak` (5 tests) |
| `crates/ai/tests/ai/mod.rs` | change | `pub mod position_model;` after `pub mod observe_instance_data;` |

Do not touch: `crates/engine/`, `crates/cards/`, `crates/luau/`, `crates/ai/src/lethal.rs` (its visited set follows the signature), `crates/ai/src/config.rs`, `crates/ai/generation.json`, `spec/`, `apps/`. No ruling: §4.3, §4.4 and §4.5 step 4 settle every case. Governing: §4.2 step 3, §4.3, §4.4, §4.5, §9.9, R1224, R783000, R346, R1361, R63, R78.

## Steps

0. Before any edit: `cargo build --release -p jackioh-tools && cp target/release/jackioh ~/control-jackioh`.

1. `simulate.rs`, above `card_signature`:
```rust
/// `items` sorted and joined by commas: a part of `search_signature` that two orders of the same moves
/// must sign alike.
fn sorted(items: impl Iterator<Item = String>) -> String {
    let mut items: Vec<String> = items.collect();
    items.sort();
    items.join(",")
}

/// What rides a card through its zones and changes how it plays later (#898): its memory, keys sorted
/// so the order a script wrote them in splits nothing, and its tuning (B3.4, R386). Each only when it
/// holds something, so a card without them signs as before.
fn rides_signature(card: &CardInstance) -> String {
    let mut signature = String::new();
    if !card.memory.is_empty() {
        let memory = sorted(card.memory.iter().map(|(key, value)| format!("{key}={value}")));
        signature.push_str(&format!(";m{memory}"));
    }
    if let Some(tuning) = &card.tuning {
        signature.push_str(&format!(";t{tuning:?}"));
    }
    signature
}
```
In `card_signature`, first add `let enchantments = match &card.enchantments { Some(enchantments) if !enchantments.is_empty() => format!(";e{enchantments:?}"), _ => String::new() };`. Then change the format string to `"{}={}{}{}/{:?}{}{enchantments}"`, with `rides_signature(card)` as its last argument. Update its doc: it now also covers cards in a graveyard, an exile or a pile, plus what rides them. In `unit_play_signature`, append `{}` to the format string and `rides_signature(unit)` to the arguments. Its enchantments are already signed.

2. `simulate.rs`, after `unit_play_signature`, add `push_side_parts`. Its doc says the parts are pushed only when not the default, as R1224's debt is, and kept order-free (sorted, the engine's sequence ids left out):
```rust
fn push_side_parts(state: &GameState, player: PlayerId, parts: &mut Vec<String>) {
    let side = &state.players[player];
    let mana = &side.mana;
    if mana.max != max_mana_for(side) || mana.next_turn_mod != 0 || mana.perm_mod != 0 {
        parts.push(format!("M{player}{}/{}/{}", mana.max, mana.next_turn_mod, mana.perm_mod));
    }
    if side.locks.units.iter().chain(&side.locks.backrow).any(|locked| *locked) {
        parts.push(format!("L{player}{:?}/{:?}", side.locks.units, side.locks.backrow));
    }
    if !side.mods.is_empty() {
        let mods = sorted(side.mods.iter().map(|modifier| format!("{:?}{:?}", modifier.expiry, modifier.kind)));
        parts.push(format!("X{player}{mods}"));
    }
    let log = &side.turn_log;
    if *log != TurnLog::default() {
        let mut costs = log.costs_paid.clone().unwrap_or_default();
        costs.sort_unstable();
        parts.push(format!(
            "T{player}{}:{}:{costs:?}:{}:{:?}/{:?}/{:?}",
            log.cards_played,
            sorted(log.played_ids.iter().cloned()),
            sorted(log.played_by_type.iter().flatten().map(|(kind, count)| format!("{kind:?}{count}"))),
            log.mana_borrowed,
            log.borrowed_parts,
            log.mana_locked,
        ));
    }
    if side.fatigue_count != 0 {
        parts.push(format!("F{player}{}", side.fatigue_count));
    }
    if let Some(jade) = side.jade {
        parts.push(format!("J{player}{jade}"));
    }
    if let Some(extra) = side.extra_turns {
        parts.push(format!("E{player}{extra}"));
    }
    if let Some(cap) = side.hand_cap {
        parts.push(format!("C{player}{cap}"));
    }
    if !side.graveyard.is_empty() {
        parts.push(format!("G{player}{}", sorted(side.graveyard.iter().map(card_signature))));
    }
    if !side.exile.is_empty() {
        parts.push(format!("Y{player}{}", sorted(side.exile.iter().map(card_signature))));
    }
    if let Some(piles) = &side.backrow_piles
        && piles.iter().any(|pile| !pile.is_empty())
    {
        let piles = piles
            .iter()
            .map(|pile| pile.iter().map(card_signature).collect::<Vec<_>>().join(","))
            .collect::<Vec<_>>()
            .join("/");
        parts.push(format!("P{player}{piles}"));
    }
}
```

3. `search_signature`: in the `for player in PLAYER_IDS` loop, after `parts.push(format!("b{backrow}"));`, call `push_side_parts(state, player, &mut parts);`. After the `owed` block, add this, with a `// #898:` comment saying the same rule applies:
```rust
    if !state.delayed.is_empty() {
        let delayed = sorted(state.delayed.iter().map(|entry| {
            format!(
                "{}{:?}{:?}{:?}{:?}{:?}",
                entry.owner, entry.at, entry.not_before, entry.resume, entry.watch, entry.hand_watch
            )
        }));
        parts.push(format!("D{delayed}"));
    }
    if let Some(marks) = &state.marks
        && !marks.is_empty()
    {
        let marks = sorted(marks.iter().map(|mark| format!("{}:{}:{}", mark.instance_id, mark.mark, mark.color)));
        parts.push(format!("K{marks}"));
    }
```
Extend the doc comment with the new parts. Add `TurnLog` and `max_mana_for` to the `use jackioh_engine::{…}`. Run `cargo fmt`.

4. Write `mod signature` (§Tests) and run it. Then `cargo build --release -p jackioh-tools && cp target/release/jackioh ~/signature-jackioh`. Start screen 1 in the background from the repo root: `~/signature-jackioh arena --a self --b bin:~/control-jackioh --set improve-dev > ~/screen-signature.log 2>&1`.

